      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There are three key factors to adjust: ensure your iron reaches 380-400°F, increase the pressure significantly by pressing down firmly, and extend the cycle to 24–30 seconds. Additionally, verify that your polyester fabric has adequate thermal stability (high-end polyester) and that you are not overheating it, which occurs when the fabric is pre-calibrated to a specific temperature or if the ambient temperature is too high. Make sure to perform a quick temperature check on a scrap piece before attempting a full production run.",
