    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The random blotching likely indicates that a protective plate (Teflon sheet or heat press matting) is touching the print at irregular points, preventing heat transfer in those specific areas. This could happen if the platen isn't perfectly flat, the arm on a swing-away press isn't centered, or if there is dust or residue on the surface creating resistance to uniform contact. Since the ink isn't settling uniformly, check for micro-scratches or debris on your platen that might be blocking heat flow in certain spots. Always press directly onto the platen without any intermediate sheets if your transfers are designed for that, or ensure all protective layers are perfectly aligned.",
